{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-09f56cd3ee0b9c3c1d39","statement":"Let $1\\leq k<l\\leq m+n$, then\n\n- $(u-v)[d_k(u),y_{k}(v)]=(-1)^{\\bk}(y_k(u)d_k(v)-y_k(v)d_k(u))$,\n\n- $(u-v)[d_k(u),x_{k}(v)]=(-1)^{\\bk}(x_k(v)d_k(u)-x_k(u)d_k(v))$,\n\n- $y_k(u)d_k(v)-y_k(v)d_k(u)=d_k(v)y_k(u)-d_k(u)y_k(v)$,\n\n- $x_k(v)d_k(u)-x_k(u)d_k(v)=d_k(u)x_k(v)-d_k(v)x_k(u)$,\n\n- $[d_k(u),x_l(v)]=[d_k(u),y_l(v)]=0$.","source_id":"arXiv:2604.25462","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"08b79f43b8e26fb69aab495e7183d9890dd588cdf79d135b252c6fbc5fc589c3","kind":"lemma","label":"Lemma 1","ref_key":"lem:com1","name":"","order":20,"deps":[],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.25462","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"6be317c9138164c30aa47ee14fa526a73ac66be915e144fb042815ac3c6611f7","line":820,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-29T14:23:03+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v3","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":319,"math_hints":26}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:2604.25462","title":"Representations of Super Yangians with Gelfand-Tsetlin bases","abstract":"The evaluation homomorphism from the super Yangian $\\mathrm Y(\\mathfrak{gl}_{m|n})$ to the universal enveloping algebra $\\mathrm U(\\mathfrak{gl}_{m|n})$ allows one to regard the $\\mathfrak{gl}_{m|n}$-modules as $\\mathrm Y(\\mathfrak{gl}_{m|n})$-modules. In this paper, we establish necessary and sufficient conditions for simple tensor products of covariant evaluation modules to be tame. We also provide an explicit construction of Gelfand-Tsetlin bases for tensor products of skew modules.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Zheng Li","Jian Zhang"],"year":"2026","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.25462","cluster":"representation_theory","macros":{"End":"{\\rm{End}\\ts}","ot":"\\otimes","la":"\\lambda","La":"\\Lambda","al":"\\alpha","be":"\\beta","ga":"\\gamma","Ga":